1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:23,073
Aurelio pointed the gun at the key. That told me everything. Not at
the driver who had beaten him. Not at the police coming through his
gates. At the little gold object that would make it impossible for him
to keep pretending his promises were only decorations. Nobody touches
it, he said. Lord Orlan froze with the case in his hands.

2
00:00:23,323 --> 00:00:47,732
I stood three steps away. Behind me, Shawna moved toward Rosa and the
others. Not running. Making room. Keeping the people she loved out of
the line the duke was trying to draw through the courtyard. I could
feel the thunder's cost in my legs. I had no more to spend. Nigga, I
still had me. You lost, I said. Aurelio laughed. It sounded painful.

3
00:00:47,982 --> 00:01:09,260
I built this. Nigga, half the men you stole it from standing behind
me. He glanced toward Nero and Celadon. Looked away quickly. You think
they made it beautiful? They made boats. Cars. Little races for men
who wanted trophies cheap enough to carry home. I made kings come
here. And one came. His eyes hit mine.

4
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:31,889
The stranger in the dark uniform stood beside the palace door,
watching us with his hands clasped behind his back. He had moved out
of the gun's line without seeming to move at all. His attention
bothered me more than the weapon. But Aurelio had the weapon. One
nigga at a time. You walked into my harbor, the duke said. You wrecked
my boats.

5
00:01:32,139 --> 00:01:55,892
You humiliated my men. You took my guests, my drivers, my staff—
Nigga, listen to how much of your sentence is people. They were mine.
No. He shook the gun toward me. They came because I paid. They stayed
because I came back. The courtyard went quiet. Aurelio looked past me
at the crowd beyond the gates. Workers. Drivers. Musicians.

6
00:01:56,142 --> 00:02:18,250
Islanders who had followed the final race into the palace square and
now stood watching the man whose name had been over every door they
entered. Some of them had spent years lowering their eyes when he
passed. They weren't lowering them now. You think they love you? he
asked again. I smiled faintly. Nigga, you already asked that. Answer
got louder.

7
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:41,648
A hand touched his shoulder. The stranger in the dark uniform. Put it
down, Aurelio. The duke jerked away. Don't tell me what to do in my
own house. The stranger removed his hand. Then finish your lesson. He
stepped back. Nigga, I did not like him at all. Aurelio turned toward
Lord Orlan. Give me the case. Orlan's hands shook.

8
00:02:41,898 --> 00:03:04,347
He looked at the gun. Then at me. Then, very carefully, he placed the
case on the ground between us and stepped away from it. The duke's
face changed. Another man had chosen. He fired. The shot struck the
stone beside Orlan's foot. Orlan fell backward. The crowd screamed.
Knox shouted. I moved. Not thunder. Me.

9
00:03:04,597 --> 00:03:27,795
I crossed the last steps and struck Aurelio's gun arm upward as he
fired again. The bullet shattered a palace window. I drove him against
the stair rail, his shoulder hitting stone, and we went down together
with the gun trapped between our bodies. He was stronger than he
looked. Anger can lend a nigga strength too. It just charges interest
in judgment.

10
00:03:28,045 --> 00:03:49,633
He hit my ribs. The old wound flared. I answered with an elbow and
felt him gasp. His gun came free for half a second. I caught his wrist
and slammed it against the rail until the weapon fell between the
steps. He kicked me hard enough to break my balance. I went onto one
knee. Aurelio ran. Up the palace stairs.

11
00:03:49,883 --> 00:04:14,766
Through the open doors. Past the stranger, who moved aside and let him
go with an expression almost like disappointment. I followed. Shawna
called my name behind me. I looked back once. She stood beside Knox,
gun lowered, eyes on mine. Come back, she said. Nigga, always. Then I
went into the palace. Aurelio had built the interior to make a man
feel small.

12
00:04:15,016 --> 00:04:39,852
High ceilings. Marble floors. Portraits twice the size of the people
they described. Gold everywhere, even on things nobody needed to look
at. He ran through it like a man fleeing his own advertisement. I
chased him past a fountain full of blue stones and into a gallery
lined with cars. His private collection. Ferraris. Bentleys. A gold
roadster.

13
00:04:40,102 --> 00:05:01,850
A black racing machine on a raised platform beneath a portrait of him
holding a falcon. Nigga had made the bird look impressed too. He
reached the black car and pulled open its door. I caught the edge
before he closed it. He struck my hand with the frame. Pain shot up my
arm. I let go. The engine started.

14
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:26,206
Aurelio looked at me through the windshield. For a second he smiled
again. Then he drove straight at me. I jumped onto the raised platform
beside the gold roadster. His car tore past, struck a display stand
and smashed through the gallery's glass doors into the inner
courtyard. Nigga had finally joined me in respecting architecture
creatively. I went after him.

15
00:05:26,456 --> 00:05:48,666
Outside, the black car spun around the courtyard fountain. A narrow
ramp climbed toward the palace's upper terrace, wide enough for one
vehicle. Aurelio took it, tires shrieking, heading for the private
road beyond the northern wall. He had a way out. I had a gold roadster
with its keys still hanging from a little ceremonial hook.

16
00:05:48,916 --> 00:06:11,784
Some rich niggas mistake display for security right up to the end. I
started it and drove through the broken doors. The roadster roared
beneath me, engine huge, hood long and bright as sunrise. I hit the
ramp behind Aurelio and climbed through a storm of dust and broken
stone. The palace courtyard fell away below.

17
00:06:12,034 --> 00:06:35,210
Ahead, his black car reached the terrace and turned toward the outer
gate. I came alongside at the top. There was barely room. He looked
over, and I saw the exact moment he realized I was driving one of his
favorite cars. Nigga, I said through the open side, you got good taste
in defeat. He rammed me. The roadster struck the terrace wall.

18
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:55,818
Stone broke away. Beyond it lay the lower gardens, a long drop broken
by cypress trees and statues of men who had never had to fight me. I
held the wheel. He hit me again. The gold car's front wheel climbed
the low wall. For a breath I looked down at the gardens beneath my
door.

19
00:06:56,068 --> 00:07:16,238
Then I turned into him, hard enough to catch his front corner and
force his black car sideways across the narrow terrace. Both engines
screamed. The cars locked together. We slid toward the fountain at the
terrace's center and struck it in a crash that threw water over both
windshields. The engines died.

20
00:07:16,488 --> 00:07:39,895
Nigga, we had reached the end of the road in a very expensive manner.
I got out slowly. My legs shook. My hand burned. Blood ran from a cut
at my hairline into one eye. I wiped it away and saw Aurelio climbing
from the black car, a pistol in his hand. Another one. The nigga owned
backups for everything except character. He aimed.

21
00:07:40,145 --> 00:07:57,480
I went behind the roadster as the shot tore through its open door.
Gold paint flew. I drew my own gun, came up on the other side and held
him in my sights. For the first time we stood still together. The sea
spread behind him. The island lay below.

22
00:07:57,730 --> 00:08:19,378
He looked around as if hoping the palace, the cars, the whole
brilliant thing he had built around himself might speak on his behalf.
Nothing did. You could have taken the money, he said. Nigga, I got
money. The ships. Got a captain for them. The women. I stared at him.
My wife chose me. That's why you don't understand any of this.

23
00:08:19,628 --> 00:08:42,829
His face twisted. You are nothing but noise. I thought of the harbor
crowd. Of the band changing its song when I stepped off the ferry. Of
Rosa singing after the attack. Of Shawna filling an empty opera house
with a voice big enough to make it hers before I owned a single stone.
I smiled. Nigga, you heard me coming. Aurelio fired.

24
00:08:43,079 --> 00:09:06,076
I fired back. His shot struck the fountain beside me. Mine struck him
in the chest. He took one step backward. Then another. The gun fell
from his hand. He sat down heavily against the broken edge of the
fountain, green racing suit darkening, eyes fixed on the palace doors.
I kept my weapon trained on him until he stopped moving.

25
00:09:06,326 --> 00:09:32,192
Aurelio Cruel died looking toward a house that no longer answered him.
No speech at the end. No secret son. No last contract. No letter
explaining that he had loved somebody too much to stop being cruel.
Just a man who had finally run out of people between himself and the
consequences. I lowered my gun. My hand shook. Footsteps came from the
terrace stairs.

26
00:09:32,442 --> 00:09:54,447
Shawna reached me first. She looked at the duke, then at my face, then
put both arms around me so hard I let the weight of my body settle
against hers. You came back, she whispered. Nigga, I took the scenic
route. She laughed once through the tears in her eyes. Then she kissed
me. Tank came up behind her with Knox and Odette.

27
00:09:54,697 --> 00:10:19,183
He looked at the two wrecked cars, the broken fountain, the duke and
me. Nigga, he said slowly, you cannot be trusted with a tour. I
laughed. It hurt. I laughed anyway. Odette checked Aurelio. Stood.
Nodded once to Knox. The duke was dead. Below us, the palace gates
opened fully. His remaining guards had laid down their weapons. Some
because they were frightened.

28
00:10:19,433 --> 00:10:39,254
Some because they had been waiting for a reason. Some because the man
who had paid them was dead and the man who had beaten him stood above
them with his wife in his arms, looking like a future they wanted to
survive into. I didn't pretend all those reasons were the same. I
accepted the guns off the road.

29
00:10:39,503 --> 00:10:58,979
Lord Orlan waited at the foot of the stairs with the seventh key. This
time his hands didn't shake. He held it out to me. Tank looked at the
case, then at me. "Nigga, count them." "Seven," I said. "Count the
niggas who tried to stop you." "Nigga, I need dinner first." Porsche
laughed.

30
00:10:59,229 --> 00:11:24,434
"That nigga's list needs a table." Mercedes opened the key case wider.
"Give the man room. Nigga just won a country-shaped honeymoon." Shawna
took my uninjured hand. "He won a bed before he wins anything else
tonight." "That nigga deserves a bed," Tank said solemnly. "Several,"
Bruno added. I looked at my wife. "One. Correct company." She kissed
me, and the niggas stopped counting.

31
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:46,912
The final key, he said. To Captain Aiden. Winner of the Grand Prix of
Kings. The courtyard began cheering before he finished. I took the
key. Marcellus came forward through the crowd, examined it for one
second and nodded. Still opens, he said. Nigga, you proud? Of the
workmanship? Certainly. I laughed and hugged him with one arm.

32
00:11:47,162 --> 00:12:10,592
The stranger in the dark uniform stood near the palace doors. He
watched me holding the seventh key. Then he inclined his head, turned
and walked away through a side entrance with two men following him. I
remembered his face. But the crowd was calling my name. My wife was
holding my hand. The island had opened its gates. Nigga, I had won.
